A||N||5||Eric_PA||How to read numbers on 3.8 block||||5||
Z||000000||Eric_PA||03-18-2001||11:44 PM||||Well, on my search this weekend to find a 4.9 Caddy V8 engine I came across a 3800 real cheap. I ended up getting it today with the wire harness and computer for under $100. I am going to tear it down and do a rebuild on it, but wondering what car this thing came out of. I will take pics and post them tomorrow. <P>Here are the numbers off of the block:<BR>There is a "6" then "3800 cc" on the block on the pulley side<BR>There is "25531617" then "4" on the block on the flywheel side.<BR>On the top of the Intake manifold on the pulley side the number "25534834" is there.<BR>Finally on the flywheel side located at the top of the block the following is listed "6" "4" "3800cc" "SGI" "kI88"<BR>I hope this isn't the 150 HP version of the 3.8. I guess if it is I can change the cam and computer.<P>Eric<P><p>[This message has been edited by Eric_PA (edited 03-18-2001).]||||reg||5
Z||000001||Eric_PA||03-19-2001||12:34 PM||||to the top  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> Still no pics.||||reg||1
Z||000002||rockcrawl||03-19-2001||07:58 PM||||Eric,<BR> Too bad you couldn't find a 4.9, but the 3.8 ain't bad either. The series I engines had staggered exhaust ports like the 2.8, and the series II had evenly spaced ports. Up until '87 there were 6 flywheel to crank bolts and no ballance shaft under the intake, starting in '88 they had 8 bolts and a ballance shaft. If it has a distributor, it's a pre-'86. I had the 150 hp '87 engine in my yellow car, it's definately a hell of a lot better than a 2.8. Here's what the '87 looks like <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/38engine_1.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||Eric_PA||03-20-2001||06:38 AM||||Thanks for that info Rock. I checked a bit more into it, it's an 88 from a Lasabre rated at 150 HP. I picked up a computer from an 89 Buick Park Avenue to use in it. I got this so that I can get the higher redline and put in a stock cam good for 170 HP. I hope that works, if not there wasn't much lost here at the price I paid. I am trying to get the Image poster program loaded in my computer so I can post a pic of it, but am having trouble intalling it. The engine I picked up has a grey plastic cover around the center of the intake wit 3800 writen in red. <BR>I was wondering, do you know where I could find performance parts for this engine? I would like to put a performnce cam and roller rockers in it like Chris West did to there 3800. And for swapping this in, it looks like an easy swap with the allready made mounts from Chris West. I know I have to get a custom flywheel, thats the biggest thing to get done. This engine will mate up to a Getrag 5 speed and once finished wil be going in my Automatic GT.<P>update:<BR>Just got home from work to take a few pics and I noticed that it has 6 flywheel bolts and the exhaust the way you described it. I thought it was an 88. I am a bit worrried now since I have no clue on what exactly I have. It doesn't have a distributor. It has the three coils mounted in front of the altenator. I wish I could post the pics so you could see it. I tried to find cams today, but can't get it until I know what I have. The engine was tagged with 88 to 91 Buick Lasabre.  <BR>Eric<P>[This message has been edited by Eric_PA (edited 03-20-2001).]<p>[This message has been edited by Eric_PA (edited 03-20-2001).]||||reg||7
